course: dictionary
lesson: 6669
title: Oat and oats
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Oat is a noun, and so is oats. An oat is a kind of cereal plant that farmers grow for its grain. Oats, usually said in the plural, means the grains from that plant. When you meet the word, check whether it means the plant or the food.
explain: Context helps you choose. «Bread fills ducks up without much goodness... peas, oats, sweetcorn and duck food are better» shows oats as food, in the same list as other things to feed ducks. «Piles of wheat, oats, barley, beech-mast and nuts lie ready to be moved» shows oats as grain, stored in heaps.
explain: Oat can also describe another word, which makes it an adjective. In «oat milk», oat tells you what kind of milk it is. Phrases like «rolled oats» and «porridge oats» mean the grains that go into your breakfast.
fact: An oat is a cereal plant grown for its grain.
fact: Oats are the grains from this plant, used to make porridge, oatcakes, flapjacks and muesli.
fact: Oats are also used to feed horses.
fact: Oats are a healthy wholegrain food that gives slow energy.
fact: Oats are a crop that grows in cool, damp places.
exercise: «Peas, oats, sweetcorn and duck food are better, in small amounts.» In this sentence, what are oats? | A plant growing in a field | *Food that is good for ducks | A kind of pond | A type of bread
exercise: Mum adds «rolled oats» to the pan. What are rolled oats? | A bowl for breakfast | A plant with long leaves | A kind of biscuit | *Oat grains, flattened for cooking
exercise: Find the word in «oat milk» that tells you what kind of milk it is. | milk | the | *oat | is
test: Oats are a healthy wholegrain food that gives what kind of energy? | Fast, sudden energy | Energy only from sweets | *Slow energy | No energy at all
test: In science lessons, where does the oat crop grow best? | *In cool, damp places | In hot, dry deserts | Under the sea | Inside a city building
exam: «A bowl of breakfast can come from all over the world: oats from a cold, wet field, bananas from a warm tropical farm, and milk from a cow on a farm close by.» Where do the oats come from? | A cow on a farm close by | A warm tropical farm | *A cold, wet field | A bowl at breakfast
